{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01718",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 4.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "come in, have a seat by the desk"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.47,
      "end_seconds": 7.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Hello, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.52,
      "end_seconds": 13.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.4,
      "end_seconds": 21.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "okay, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. Tell me what's brought you in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.92,
      "end_seconds": 27.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "I've been dealing with red sore skin on my shoulders."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.65,
      "end_seconds": 34.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.19,
      "end_seconds": 43.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "It's, It's been three days now. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.84,
      "end_seconds": 54.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.28,
      "end_seconds": 62.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "I notice it more with clothes rubbing. It settles a little with cool showers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.54,
      "end_seconds": 71.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "And, And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 71.23,
      "end_seconds": 76.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.75,
      "end_seconds": 93.6,
      "duration_seconds": 15.85,
      "text": "I was getting to that! As for tightness of the skin, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.63,
      "end_seconds": 98.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Alright, how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.5,
      "end_seconds": 103.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "I'd say on and off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.7,
      "end_seconds": 108.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.93,
      "end_seconds": 115.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kinda... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.19,
      "end_seconds": 122.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.18,
      "end_seconds": 130.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "about a six out of ten i've also had a little peeling, since yesterday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.53,
      "end_seconds": 136.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.53,
      "end_seconds": 144.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kinda... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.82,
      "end_seconds": 151.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.45,
      "text": "take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.99,
      "end_seconds": 155.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I'd give it a six, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 157.37,
      "end_seconds": 159.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.43,
      "end_seconds": 165.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "So, any vomiting, fever or blisters at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.77,
      "end_seconds": 171.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "ah, no vomiting, fever or blisters, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.25,
      "end_seconds": 177.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "What about headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.56,
      "end_seconds": 181.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.53,
      "end_seconds": 185.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.3,
      "end_seconds": 188.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "no, joints are fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.57,
      "end_seconds": 192.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.18,
      "end_seconds": 195.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "bowels are regular, nothing odd"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.66,
      "end_seconds": 201.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "alright, has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.76,
      "end_seconds": 204.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "I've had migraines, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.09,
      "end_seconds": 206.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "Mm-hmm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.0,
      "end_seconds": 212.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "I've had COPD for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.88,
      "end_seconds": 214.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.76,
      "end_seconds": 220.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "An irregular heartbeat, for two years. I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.52,
      "end_seconds": 221.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.62,
      "end_seconds": 233.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.06,
      "end_seconds": 239.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.54,
      "end_seconds": 243.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.89,
      "end_seconds": 252.56,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "Yes, I had a cataract operation in my left eye, about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.1,
      "end_seconds": 255.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.83,
      "end_seconds": 261.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "It's sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, maybe, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.62,
      "end_seconds": 267.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.14,
      "end_seconds": 294.35,
      "duration_seconds": 25.21,
      "text": "not with me i'll bring it next time i'm on Tiotropium inhaler, once a day i did try to ignore it for a while. Apixaban i take it 5 milligrams, twice a day for the heart rhythm. Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.91,
      "end_seconds": 299.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.4,
      "end_seconds": 311.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "uh, yes, cat fur, it gives me sneezing i'm allergic to nickel, I get a rash on my skin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.61,
      "end_seconds": 317.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.3,
      "end_seconds": 333.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.47,
      "end_seconds": 360.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Okay: respiratory rate 17, temperature 36.7. And oxygen saturation is 97 percent, heart rate 77, blood pressure 113 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.12,
      "end_seconds": 366.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.17,
      "end_seconds": 371.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.94,
      "end_seconds": 382.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "the skin is pink and tender with no blistering"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.88,
      "end_seconds": 387.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.92,
      "end_seconds": 408.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "so, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is mild sunburn"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.43,
      "end_seconds": 412.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.51,
      "end_seconds": 439.75,
      "duration_seconds": 25.24,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like mild sunburn. Cool compresses, moisturiser and stay out of the sun for a few days. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Come back if blisters develop. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 440.82,
      "end_seconds": 444.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}